# IYDT-GSRP seismic-acoustic MultiPEM analysis

`I-SUGAR-hob-0` is a two-stage rapid assessment that combines seismic and
acoustic observations to infer SUGAR log-yield and HOB.

## Native prerequisites

From this directory create the prior-code and optimization directories:

```text
ln -s ../../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp/Phenomenology Code
mkdir -p Opt
```

Run the single-phenomenology calibrations first, then stage their MLE results:

```text
cp ../Seismic/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_1_0.RData
cp ../Acoustic/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_2_0.RData
```

These files are required by the shipped deck's `opt_files_in`; missing or
misnamed files cause `readRDS` to fail.

## Run sequence

```text
cd I-SUGAR-hob-0
R CMD BATCH runMPEM.r runMPEM.out &
```

After the background calibration finishes successfully:

```text
cp .RData .RData-calibration
R CMD BATCH runMPEM_0.r runMPEM_0.out &
```

Retain `.RData-calibration` as the pristine MultiPEM calibration for all future
event analyses; never replace it with the event-modified `.RData`. The
MultiPEM calibration also writes its own `opt.RData`.

## Docker

Single-phenomenology Docker outputs reside in separate job snapshots. Copy each
source `opt.RData` from
`RESULTS/work/IYDT-gsrp/PHENOMENOLOGY/ANALYSIS/opt.RData` to the two canonical
destinations above, then create the MultiPEM job:

```text
Rscript mpem.R run IYDT-gsrp/2-Phen-sa/I-SUGAR-hob-0
```

Do not reuse a single-phenomenology results directory for this analysis; the
launcher correctly rejects cross-analysis reuse.
